.lattice/story/actives/B-2296/review-runs.json:15:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"73dcd6e40d6f177c841e3d577bc3ff29b1d6a227279f9e4eef253d452c33d333\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Add a snapshot/binding record for a checklist userSees claim: { normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash, attestedAt, attestedBy? }. Reuse existing freshness primitives (currentMaterialHash / checkEvidenceFreshnessForGit in handlers/checklist.ts; storyFilesHash from B-5a9a). normalizeClaim is a pure Fn: trim, collapse internal whitespace runs to one space, strip trailing whitespace — deterministic, no semantic interpretation. Types in core/types.ts; normalize + sha256 digest in a pure fn module (no I/O).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define the frozen-claim snapshot record and a deterministic claim-normalization Fn\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the new smoke and sees \\\"normalizeClaim collapses whitespace deterministically\\\" and \\\"snapshot record binds {normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash}\\\" among the passing assertions.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"two userSees differing only in whitespace yield an IDENTICAL digest (no false drift); differing by one non-whitespace char yields a DIFFERENT digest\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"empty or whitespace-only userSees normalizes to empty and yields a stable digest without throwing\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"normalizeClaim collapses arbitrary whitespace (tabs, repeated spaces, leading/trailing) to a canonical form deterministically\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Capture the snapshot when a checklist item's userSees becomes an attested delivered claim (PLAN pins the exact hook; candidate: on checklist_update status=done). Detect drift by recomputing the normalized digest and re-checking material freshness: drift when normalizedClaimDigest changed (claim edited) OR the bound material is stale (rename-aware `git diff --name-status -M`, mirroring review_incremental_context). A userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error). Pure detection Fn + handler wiring; NO gate blocking in this story.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Snapshot userSees at attestation time and detect bidirectional drift (claim OR material), classify legacy-unbound\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the smoke and sees \\\"material drift under frozen userSees -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"userSees text edited -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"unrelated file change -> no drift\\\", and \\\"userSees with no snapshot -> legacy-unbound\\\".\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"editing userSees text after delivery (non-whitespace) is detected as driftKind=claim even with material unchanged; a whitespace-only userSees edit produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"a userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error); an unrelated non-story-owned file change produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"after userSees is snapshotted at status=done, mutating story-owned material makes detectDrift report driftKind=material with actionRequired=re_attestation\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Expose a read-only structured report: { code: 'FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT', claimRef, itemId, previousDigest, currentDigest, previousMaterialHash, currentMaterialHash, driftKind: 'claim'|'material'|'both', classification: 'bound'|'legacy-unbound', actionRequired: 're_attestation' }. Surface via a new read-only CLI (e.g. frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId) and/or fold into story_get, mirroring the B-d243/B-edf1 storyFilesHash drift-advisory. NON-blocking in Phase 1 (no recovery path yet; a gate now would wedge stories). Follow the Handler runtime-revalidation convention — re-check every schema constraint at each consumer at runtime, not only in Zod.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"CLAUDE.md\",\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Surface drift as a structured, non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory at a read point\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs `lattice frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId=B-xxxx` on a story with drifted userSees and sees a JSON advisory carrying code FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT, driftKind, and actionRequired: re_attestation; a clean story reports zero drift and exits 0.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the advisory never changes a gate verdict: running it against a drifted story does not fail review, delivery, or DONE gates (Phase 1 non-blocking invariant)\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the command is read-only: it writes no evidence or files and exits 0 for both clean and drifted stories\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId prints the structured FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory (code, claimRef, driftKind, actionRequired, classification) for a drifted story and a clean report for a clean story\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"RED-first, deterministic (no live network). Cover: (1) material drift under a frozen userSees -> detected; (2) userSees text edited -> detected; (3) unrelated file change -> NO drift (false-positive guard); (4) whitespace-only userSees edit normalizes to NO drift (false-positive guard); (5) userSees with no snapshot -> legacy-unbound. Assert the advisory is NON-blocking (does not fail any gate) in Phase 1. Register the smoke in lattice.config.json validate.commands and package.json scripts.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"RED-first smoke covering both false-positive guards; register in validate + package.json\",\"userSees\":\"`lattice validate` runs the new frozen-claim-drift smoke and reports it green among the validate commands; the smoke output shows all five cases including the two false-positive guards passing.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the smoke is deterministic and offline (no live network, no live claude -p) so it cannot flake in CI\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the two false-positive guards (unrelated-file change and whitespace-only edit both produce NO drift) are explicit assertions in the smoke\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"the frozen-claim-drift smoke runs under `node bin/lattice.js validate` and reports green, covering all five cases\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Phase 1 of the evidence-integrity program §5 follow-on (docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md §5). Bind each checklist userSees frozen claim to a snapshot { normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash, attestedAt } and surface a structured, NON-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory when EITHER the normalized claim text drifts OR the bound material drifts (rename-aware) under a frozen claim. Bidirectional binding is required because in both source incidents (F-027/F-060 userSees, F-059 plan.md) the claim text stayed frozen while the code moved, so a claim-digest-only check catches neither. Normalization is mechanical (trim + collapse whitespace); no semantic diffing. Legacy userSees with no snapshot are classified legacy-unbound and reported, never errored. Scope: userSees only. Detect + report only — the blocking gate, reviewer re-attestation recovery, and legacy migration policy are Phase 2. Reuses B-ec67 (M1) receipt/freshness and the B-5a9a/B-d243/B-edf1 storyFilesHash drift-advisory pattern.\",\"headHash\":\"21ec3653fad3bf4d4254642fe9d3b11a1d449739\",\"materialHash\":\"5a4deeb930087b4eea533ecf7c60e167f90936b03b4062826f4694e7e31056ff\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/frozen-claim-drift-check.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/**\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\".lattice/**\",\"docs/**\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/verification.ts\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"shadow\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"cfbb5076ef6f4b1a561ce0301756090ede907b205849c731054870a1b716c6fb\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"3ebaff3d646c3ffd2fe6a72e22e47a1b8fbbbfaee363e27e8299caa1a0144972\",\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"title\":\"Detect frozen-claim drift (evidence-integrity §5 follow-on, Phase 1 of 2): bind checklist userSees to a normalized claim-digest + materialHash snapshot and surface a non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory when either drifts\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.242\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-2296 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-2296\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n",
.lattice/story/actives/B-2296/review-runs.json:81:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"c916bc0a53f4c1465a605def7d6cde3601c5843e8b61475d73fa1a9b0a4d8742\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review verification intent and evidence coverage.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"9845080b4d332e675cced9230749066c0a72bab5e830d54417c7f6206a5e7dc7\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Add a snapshot/binding record for a checklist userSees claim: { normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash, attestedAt, attestedBy? }. Reuse existing freshness primitives (currentMaterialHash / checkEvidenceFreshnessForGit in handlers/checklist.ts; storyFilesHash from B-5a9a). normalizeClaim is a pure Fn: trim, collapse internal whitespace runs to one space, strip trailing whitespace — deterministic, no semantic interpretation. Types in core/types.ts; normalize + sha256 digest in a pure fn module (no I/O).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define the frozen-claim snapshot record and a deterministic claim-normalization Fn\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the new smoke and sees \\\"normalizeClaim collapses whitespace deterministically\\\" and \\\"snapshot record binds {normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash}\\\" among the passing assertions.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"two userSees differing only in whitespace yield an IDENTICAL digest (no false drift); differing by one non-whitespace char yields a DIFFERENT digest\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"empty or whitespace-only userSees normalizes to empty and yields a stable digest without throwing\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"normalizeClaim collapses arbitrary whitespace (tabs, repeated spaces, leading/trailing) to a canonical form deterministically\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Capture the snapshot when a checklist item's userSees becomes an attested delivered claim (PLAN pins the exact hook; candidate: on checklist_update status=done). Detect drift by recomputing the normalized digest and re-checking material freshness: drift when normalizedClaimDigest changed (claim edited) OR the bound material is stale (rename-aware `git diff --name-status -M`, mirroring review_incremental_context). A userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error). Pure detection Fn + handler wiring; NO gate blocking in this story.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Snapshot userSees at attestation time and detect bidirectional drift (claim OR material), classify legacy-unbound\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the smoke and sees \\\"material drift under frozen userSees -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"userSees text edited -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"unrelated file change -> no drift\\\", and \\\"userSees with no snapshot -> legacy-unbound\\\".\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"editing userSees text after delivery (non-whitespace) is detected as driftKind=claim even with material unchanged; a whitespace-only userSees edit produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"a userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error); an unrelated non-story-owned file change produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"after userSees is snapshotted at status=done, mutating story-owned material makes detectDrift report driftKind=material with actionRequired=re_attestation\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Expose a read-only structured report: { code: 'FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT', claimRef, itemId, previousDigest, currentDigest, previousMaterialHash, currentMaterialHash, driftKind: 'claim'|'material'|'both', classification: 'bound'|'legacy-unbound', actionRequired: 're_attestation' }. Surface via a new read-only CLI (e.g. frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId) and/or fold into story_get, mirroring the B-d243/B-edf1 storyFilesHash drift-advisory. NON-blocking in Phase 1 (no recovery path yet; a gate now would wedge stories). Follow the Handler runtime-revalidation convention — re-check every schema constraint at each consumer at runtime, not only in Zod.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"CLAUDE.md\",\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Surface drift as a structured, non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory at a read point\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs `lattice frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId=B-xxxx` on a story with drifted userSees and sees a JSON advisory carrying code FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT, driftKind, and actionRequired: re_attestation; a clean story reports zero drift and exits 0.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the advisory never changes a gate verdict: running it against a drifted story does not fail review, delivery, or DONE gates (Phase 1 non-blocking invariant)\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the command is read-only: it writes no evidence or files and exits 0 for both clean and drifted stories\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId prints the structured FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory (code, claimRef, driftKind, actionRequired, classification) for a drifted story and a clean report for a clean story\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"RED-first, deterministic (no live network). Cover: (1) material drift under a frozen userSees -> detected; (2) userSees text edited -> detected; (3) unrelated file change -> NO drift (false-positive guard); (4) whitespace-only userSees edit normalizes to NO drift (false-positive guard); (5) userSees with no snapshot -> legacy-unbound. Assert the advisory is NON-blocking (does not fail any gate) in Phase 1. Register the smoke in lattice.config.json validate.commands and package.json scripts.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"RED-first smoke covering both false-positive guards; register in validate + package.json\",\"userSees\":\"`lattice validate` runs the new frozen-claim-drift smoke and reports it green among the validate commands; the smoke output shows all five cases including the two false-positive guards passing.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the smoke is deterministic and offline (no live network, no live claude -p) so it cannot flake in CI\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the two false-positive guards (unrelated-file change and whitespace-only edit both produce NO drift) are explicit assertions in the smoke\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"the frozen-claim-drift smoke runs under `node bin/lattice.js validate` and reports green, covering all five cases\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Phase 1 of the evidence-integrity program §5 follow-on (docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md §5). Bind each checklist userSees frozen claim to a snapshot { normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash, attestedAt } and surface a structured, NON-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory when EITHER the normalized claim text drifts OR the bound material drifts (rename-aware) under a frozen claim. Bidirectional binding is required because in both source incidents (F-027/F-060 userSees, F-059 plan.md) the claim text stayed frozen while the code moved, so a claim-digest-only check catches neither. Normalization is mechanical (trim + collapse whitespace); no semantic diffing. Legacy userSees with no snapshot are classified legacy-unbound and reported, never errored. Scope: userSees only. Detect + report only — the blocking gate, reviewer re-attestation recovery, and legacy migration policy are Phase 2. Reuses B-ec67 (M1) receipt/freshness and the B-5a9a/B-d243/B-edf1 storyFilesHash drift-advisory pattern.\",\"headHash\":\"21ec3653fad3bf4d4254642fe9d3b11a1d449739\",\"materialHash\":\"5a4deeb930087b4eea533ecf7c60e167f90936b03b4062826f4694e7e31056ff\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/frozen-claim-drift-check.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/**\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\".lattice/**\",\"docs/**\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/verification.ts\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"shadow\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"cfbb5076ef6f4b1a561ce0301756090ede907b205849c731054870a1b716c6fb\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"3ebaff3d646c3ffd2fe6a72e22e47a1b8fbbbfaee363e27e8299caa1a0144972\",\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"title\":\"Detect frozen-claim drift (evidence-integrity §5 follow-on, Phase 1 of 2): bind checklist userSees to a normalized claim-digest + materialHash snapshot and surface a non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory when either drifts\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.242\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-test-coverage, review story B-2296 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-2296\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-test-coverage/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-test-coverage.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-test-coverage\ndescription: REVIEW phase reviewer that audits coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Read, Glob, Grep, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\nYou are `lattice-review-test-coverage`. Your duty is to inherit the value of the old `TEST_CASE_REVIEW`, but without resurrecting the old phase: you only review during the REVIEW phase whether the `verificationIntent` on the checklist is covered by valid `verificationEvidence`.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe main agent will give you a storyId. First read:\n\n```bash\nlattice story_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"detail\":true}'\nlattice checklist_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\"}'\nlattice validate '{\"story\":\"<ID>\",\"json\":true}'\n```\n\n## Review Rules\n\n1. For every checklist item, check whether the happy / edge / adversarial intent columns match the current channel:\n   - normal / high-risk / strict: all three columns should exist.\n   - fast / express: at least the happy path should be explainable; missing edge/adversarial may be advisory.\n2. For every intent with priority=`must`, there must be one valid evidence:\n   - `logic_test` / `integration_test` / `browser_test` / `docs_check` / `manual_transcript` whose `result` must not be `fail`.\n   - `waiver` must have a clear note explaining why this story should not be covered by automation.\n3. Evidence must concretely correspond to an intent; broad descriptions such as \"validate passed\" without saying which behavior is covered are not accepted.\n4. If a gap is found, write a finding with `lattice finding_add`:\n\n```bash\nlattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"desc\":\"CHK-001:edge:0 lacks valid verificationEvidence; current evidence only covers the happy path\",\"files\":[\"validate.ts\"]}'\n```\n\n## Output\n\nAt the end, output:\n\n- Coverage summary: total intent count, must-gap count, waiver count.\n- List of finding ids that were written.\n- If there are no findings, you must call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"note\":\"test coverage review passed: verified coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence, no blocker.\"}'`, then clearly state that the test coverage review passed.\n",
