text.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/frozen-claim-drift-check.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/frozen-claim-drift.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/**\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/frozen-claim-drift-smoke.ts\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\".lattice/**\",\"docs/**\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/verification.ts\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"shadow\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"cfbb5076ef6f4b1a561ce0301756090ede907b205849c731054870a1b716c6fb\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"3ebaff3d646c3ffd2fe6a72e22e47a1b8fbbbfaee363e27e8299caa1a0144972\",\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"title\":\"Detect frozen-claim drift (evidence-integrity §5 follow-on, Phase 1 of 2): bind checklist userSees to a normalized claim-digest + materialHash snapshot and surface a non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory when either drifts\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.242\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-quality, review story B-2296 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-2296\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-quality/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-2296/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-quality.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-quality\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-2296\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-quality\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-quality\ndescription: REVIEW audit: code quality (dead code / type safety / I/O isolation)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing the first-pass checks)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs newly added in CLAUDE.md / README — all must be cross-checked against the code for corresponding implementations. If you find \"promised but undelivered\" → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou do only one thing: review the code quality of changes in `git diff main...HEAD`.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --name-only` to get the list of changed files\n2. Only review changed files (don't review unchanged ones)\n3. For each file, check the following items\n\n## Check Items\n\n### 1. Dead Code\n- Modules imported but unused\n- Functions/variables defined but never called\n- Commented-out code blocks (should be deleted, not commented)\n\n### 2. Type Safety\n- Unnecessary `as any` (when a specific type could be used instead)\n- `try {} catch {}` missing error handling (empty catch swallowing errors)\n\n### 3. I/O Shell Isolation (if the project has bridge.ts)\n- Whether shell files (shells/ or ui.ts / main.ts) directly import fn.ts\n- Should interact via bridge\n\n### 4. Proof Metadata Review Coverage (narrow correctness rule)\nWhen the diff touches proof/receipt/provider/run/job metadata semantics, check\nthat any server-authored proof keys are authored and validated across both\njob.metadata and linked run.metadata (`job.metadata` and the linked\n`run.metadata` object). In this narrow review case, checking only one location is insufficient:\na proof key present only in job.metadata or only in linked run.metadata does not\nprove the other surface is fresh, server-authored, or bound to the same event;\nclient-controlled or stale metadata cannot satisfy a server-authored proof\nrequirement. This is correctness review guidance only; it is not receipt-backed production proof,\nand the reviewer must not describe it as receipt-backed production evidence.\n\n## Output\n\n```bash\nlattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"quality-cleanup: file.ts:42 imports unused-module but does not use it\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-quality\"}'\n```\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, not the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- The corresponding section of plan.md (if any)\n- Necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Prohibited**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — infer only from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist claims)\n- If the input is insufficient to make a judgment, raise a medium finding explaining what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only raise findings, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is prohibited. An unregistered finding is equivalent to not having discovered it.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-quality\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if the code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and you must return to DEV for fixes and commit, then re-enter a new round via DEV→REVIEW. Do not rerun it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, do not use `finding_add` to fake a pass; you must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason there are no blockers.\n- When starting the review for the current REVIEW round, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` calls in this round must include this field.\n- Example of recording a pass with no blockers: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Only review changed files, not the entire repository\n- Every finding must include a file path + line number\n- Do not raise pure style issues (indentation, naming preferences); only focus on issues that affect correctness and maintainability\n",
.lattice/story/actives/B-2296/review-runs.json:213:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"73dcd6e40d6f177c841e3d577bc3ff29b1d6a227279f9e4eef253d452c33d333\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Add a snapshot/binding record for a checklist userSees claim: { normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash, attestedAt, attestedBy? }. Reuse existing freshness primitives (currentMaterialHash / checkEvidenceFreshnessForGit in handlers/checklist.ts; storyFilesHash from B-5a9a). normalizeClaim is a pure Fn: trim, collapse internal whitespace runs to one space, strip trailing whitespace — deterministic, no semantic interpretation. Types in core/types.ts; normalize + sha256 digest in a pure fn module (no I/O).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define the frozen-claim snapshot record and a deterministic claim-normalization Fn\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the new smoke and sees \\\"normalizeClaim collapses whitespace deterministically\\\" and \\\"snapshot record binds {normalizedClaimDigest, materialHash, headHash}\\\" among the passing assertions.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"two userSees differing only in whitespace yield an IDENTICAL digest (no false drift); differing by one non-whitespace char yields a DIFFERENT digest\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"empty or whitespace-only userSees normalizes to empty and yields a stable digest without throwing\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"normalizeClaim collapses arbitrary whitespace (tabs, repeated spaces, leading/trailing) to a canonical form deterministically\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Capture the snapshot when a checklist item's userSees becomes an attested delivered claim (PLAN pins the exact hook; candidate: on checklist_update status=done). Detect drift by recomputing the normalized digest and re-checking material freshness: drift when normalizedClaimDigest changed (claim edited) OR the bound material is stale (rename-aware `git diff --name-status -M`, mirroring review_incremental_context). A userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error). Pure detection Fn + handler wiring; NO gate blocking in this story.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Snapshot userSees at attestation time and detect bidirectional drift (claim OR material), classify legacy-unbound\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs the smoke and sees \\\"material drift under frozen userSees -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"userSees text edited -> FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT\\\", \\\"unrelated file change -> no drift\\\", and \\\"userSees with no snapshot -> legacy-unbound\\\".\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"editing userSees text after delivery (non-whitespace) is detected as driftKind=claim even with material unchanged; a whitespace-only userSees edit produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"a userSees with no snapshot is classified legacy-unbound (not drift, not error); an unrelated non-story-owned file change produces NO drift\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"after userSees is snapshotted at status=done, mutating story-owned material makes detectDrift report driftKind=material with actionRequired=re_attestation\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Expose a read-only structured report: { code: 'FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT', claimRef, itemId, previousDigest, currentDigest, previousMaterialHash, currentMaterialHash, driftKind: 'claim'|'material'|'both', classification: 'bound'|'legacy-unbound', actionRequired: 're_attestation' }. Surface via a new read-only CLI (e.g. frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId) and/or fold into story_get, mirroring the B-d243/B-edf1 storyFilesHash drift-advisory. NON-blocking in Phase 1 (no recovery path yet; a gate now would wedge stories). Follow the Handler runtime-revalidation convention — re-check every schema constraint at each consumer at runtime, not only in Zod.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"CLAUDE.md\",\"docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Surface drift as a structured, non-blocking FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT advisory at a read point\",\"userSees\":\"A developer runs `lattice frozen_claim_drift_check --storyId=B-xxxx` on a story with drifted userSees and sees a JSON advisory carrying code FROZEN_CLAIM_DRIFT, driftKind, and actionRequired: re_attestation; a clean story reports zero drift and exits 0.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the advisory never changes a gate verdict: running it against a drifted story does not fail review, delivery, or DONE gates (Phase 1 non-blocking invariant)\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the command is read-only: it writes no evidence or files and exits 0 for both clean and drifted stories\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"frozen_claim_drif

"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-test-coverage\ndescription: REVIEW phase reviewer that audits coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Read, Glob, Grep, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\nYou are `lattice-review-test-coverage`. Your duty is to inherit the value of the old `TEST_CASE_REVIEW`, but without resurrecting the old phase: you only review during the REVIEW phase whether the `verificationIntent` on the checklist is covered by valid `verificationEvidence`.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe main agent will give you a storyId. First read:\n\n```bash\nlattice story_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"detail\":true}'\nlattice checklist_get '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\"}'\nlattice validate '{\"story\":\"<ID>\",\"json\":true}'\n```\n\n## Review Rules\n\n1. For every checklist item, check whether the happy / edge / adversarial intent columns match the current channel:\n   - normal / high-risk / strict: all three columns should exist.\n   - fast / express: at least the happy path should be explainable; missing edge/adversarial may be advisory.\n2. For every intent with priority=`must`, there must be one valid evidence:\n   - `logic_test` / `integration_test` / `browser_test` / `docs_check` / `manual_transcript` whose `result` must not be `fail`.\n   - `waiver` must have a clear note explaining why this story should not be covered by automation.\n3. Evidence must concretely correspond to an intent; broad descriptions such as \"validate passed\" without saying which behavior is covered are not accepted.\n4. If a gap is found, write a finding with `lattice finding_add`:\n\n```bash\nlattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"desc\":\"CHK-001:edge:0 lacks valid verificationEvidence; current evidence only covers the happy path\",\"files\":[\"validate.ts\"]}'\n```\n\n## Output\n\nAt the end, output:\n\n- Coverage summary: total intent count, must-gap count, waiver count.\n- List of finding ids that were written.\n- If there are no findings, you must call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"<ID>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-test-coverage\",\"note\":\"test coverage review passed: verified coverage between verificationIntent and verificationEvidence, no blocker.\"}'`, then clearly state that the test coverage review passed.\n",
