.lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/review-runs.json:15:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"73dcd6e40d6f177c841e3d577bc3ff29b1d6a227279f9e4eef253d452c33d333\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Must FAIL on current main (CLI 0.3.243, after B-506e merged at 4d417a0c4b) before any fix exists. B-506e already closed ONE class - a record that is null or a bare string now yields a typed RedEvidenceSchemaError - so do NOT include those as RED rows; they would pass and prove nothing. RECORD class still live, each verified by probe: {id:'corrupt'} versionless with no observedFailure, observedFailure of null or 123, and an ARRAY record (typeof [] is 'object', so classifyRedRecordSchemaSafe still returns 'v1' for it). ORDERING: malformed-FIRST-then-satisfying, so Array.prototype.some cannot short-circuit past it. ENVELOPE class, wholly untouched by the merge: records as {} or 42 (non-iterable TypeError) and records as 'x' (which iterates the string's characters and misreports 'a record must be an object'). SILENT class, which is NOT a crash and therefore needs a different assertion: a JSON root of [], 'x', null or 42 returns the raw value and reads as ABSENT evidence everywhere, and an unparseable file lets a raw SyntaxError escape - assert the observable wrong behaviour, not a throw. Drive everything through proofStoryDiagnosticInput then evaluateProofStoryDiagnostics, the pair the live enforce gates call, never the predicate in isolation.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/\",\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Commit a repro-first RED artifact proving both crash classes still live on current main\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Each class asserts the right shape: CRASH rows assert a bare TypeError escapes, SILENT rows assert a wrong observable value AND no throw, and the unparseable-file row asserts a RAW untyped SyntaxError escapes rather than asserting no throw.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Rows that B-506e already closed (record is null or a bare string) are absent from the artifact, so no row passes vacuously.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The committed RED artifact runs on current main and FAILS, proving all three defect classes are live before any fix exists.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"SUPERSEDES the original plan to port a harness: packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs is now ON main (it arrived with the B-506e merge) and passes there, printing 2d584cc157e83ebb2f8396735f04d46946f0ba90d18a55d9fb2f263d706a11ec. That constant is therefore main's OWN pinned value, not a foreign import, and it must NOT be re-pinned. Run it BEFORE the fix to record that it passes on the pre-fix tree; that run is the baseline CHK-007 asserts against. Its five v1-only scenarios are empty store, satisfying record, blank-observedFailure record, foreign-acceptance-target record, and mixed store, each anchored by name so the digest cannot be silently re-pinned to a different verdict. Separately: 71c267a0a7372e9679d00b84be2e2b3480151bfa88939bddcae251aa750d95bc remains a phantom produced by no artifact (audit section 7.1) and must never be pinned.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Establish the pre-fix invariance baseline from main's existing five-scenario harness\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The pinned constant is not edited, and the phantom digest 71c267a0... appears nowhere as a pinned value.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The recorded baseline names the exact commit it was taken at, so a later reader can tell whether it predates the fix.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs is run on the pre-fix tree and recorded as passing with digest 2d584cc1...\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Decision D-7. Full validation was chosen, so 'no valid verdict moved' is an assumption until this scan proves it - and the pinned digest CANNOT detect the difference, because all five of its scenarios are well-formed. Enumerate every reachable red-evidence.json in real story directories; for each record compute (current verdict, verdict under full v1 validation). The story may merge only if the differing set is empty, or