full validation rather than the rejected narrow option was implemented; a prototype-inherited observedFailure (Object.create(null) and friends) must not be accepted via the prototype chain; and an ARRAY record must be rejected, since the classifier still returns 'v1' for it. Envelope rows from acceptance section 10.2.1: E5, a JSON root that is not an object ([], 'x', null, 42) currently does NOT crash - it flows through as the raw parsed value and every consumer reads it as ABSENT evidence, making a corrupt artifact indistinguishable from a missing one, which a crash-only validator would leave untouched; E6, a missing or unknown FILE-level schemaVersion must not silently degrade to v1; E7, an unparseable file currently lets a raw SyntaxError escape from readJson and must instead produce a typed error naming the path.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence-artifact-validation.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/store.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Add fail-closed full v1 artifact validation at the read boundary with quarantine\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Malformed entries are quarantined, not dropped: the rejected entry is retained and reported with index, identifying field and reason, and an envelope fault is never reported as a record fault. An array record and a prototype-inherited observedFailure are both rejected.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Envelope rows E5, E6 and E7 each behave as specified: a non-object root is rejected rather than read as absent, a missing or unknown file-level schemaVersion does not degrade to v1, and an unparseable file yields a typed error naming the path instead of a raw SyntaxError.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"A well-formed v1 artifact loads unchanged and its gate verdict is identical to pre-fix.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Decision D-2. SUPERSEDES the earlier framing that main had no two-layer idiom to mirror: since the B-506e merge, main already classifies at the read boundary in store.ts and skips non-v1 records in the predicate. This story EXTENDS that shape rather than establishing it. The remaining hole is that the 'v1' class is RESIDUAL, not validated - classifyRedRecordSchemaSafe returns 'v1' for any object lacking a schemaVersion member without checking the legacy v1 shape, and it returns 'v1' for arrays too. So redEvidenceRecordSatisfied must never throw on arbitrary input even when a malformed record is injected directly into the diagnostic input, bypassing the read path. The audit verified observedFailure is the ONLY unguarded per-record dereference - every other check in the predicate is a truthiness test or a short-circuited read - so do not widen this into a rewrite of those checks.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/proofstory.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Extend the existing two-layer guard so the gate predicate is total on arbitrary input\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The other per-record checks are unchanged; only the missing shape guard is added, verified by diffing the predicate.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The predicate never throws even when a malformed record is injected DIRECTLY into the diagnostic input, bypassing the read boundary entirely.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The gate predicate returns a verdict for every well-formed input exactly as before.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"There are TEN production call sites on current main, not the seven this story originally claimed - the B-506e merge added three more, and the count has now been wrong TWICE from a stale inventory, so re-derive it yourself before starting. Pre-existing seven: core/machine.ts, handlers/phase-gates.ts, handlers/proofstory.ts (three sites), handlers/story-review.ts (two sites). Added by the merge, verified absent at 1847b3af6d: core/red-evidence/append.ts, and TWO sites in handlers/red-evidence.ts (that file had zero such calls before the merge). Requirements: red_evidence_get must DISPLAY the corruption rather than abort; red_evidence_add reads before appending, so it must repair-by-append or refuse with an actionable message rather than making the artifact unrepairable through the CLI; the story_review advisory path, whose catch renders 'ProofStory Diagnostics (advisory only): unavailable (<message>)', must not let corruption read as 'feature not configured'; and the three merge-added consumers must be held to the same standard. Locate all of them by symbol, never by line number.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/machine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/phase-gates.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/proofstory.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/red-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/story-review.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Make every readRedEvidence consumer surface corruption instead of aborting or degrading\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"All ten consumers are re-derived by symbol at implementation time and each renders corruption distinctly from absence; in particular the story_review advisory path does not let corruption read as 'feature not configured'.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"red_evidence_add can still repair the artifact by appending, or refuses with an actionable message naming what is wrong; it never leaves the artifact unrepairable through the CLI.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red_evidence_get displays the corruption instead of aborting, on a store carrying a malformed artifact.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Depends on the baseline recorded in CHK-002. Re-run packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs after the fix and assert it still passes with the SAME pinned digest 2d584cc157e83ebb2f8396735f04d46946f0ba90d18a55d9fb2f263d706a11ec - that is the 'no valid v1 verdict moved' proof, scoped per decision D-3 to records that are well-formed under the legacy v1 schema. If that digest moves, the fix changed a verdict it was not permitted to change; do not re-pin the constant to make it pass. Decision D-5: a blank observedFailure (empty or whitespace) is legacy-tolerated - it must keep producing UNSATISFIED with NO new diagnostic and must never be quarantined, because scenario 3 of that harness depends on exactly that report shape; this is the single sub-case where quarantine is overridden. Register the new tests in lattice.config.json validate.commands alongside the existing red-evidence smokes.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"lattice.config.json\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-007\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Assert the invariance digest is unchanged post-fix and register the regressions in validate\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"If the digest moves, it is treated as a defect in the fix; the constant is not re-pinned to make the test pass.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A blank observedFailure still produces UNSATISFIED with no new diagnostic and is never quarantined, so scenario 3's report shape is unchanged.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs passes post-fix with the SAME pinned digest as the CHK-002 baseline.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Every other item cites decisions D-1 through D-8 and section numbers of docs/requirements/decisions/red-evidence-legacy-v1-record-validation-audit.md, which is NOT on main and would otherwise be a dangling reference for anyone reading this story independently, including the PLAN scope reviewer that reads the decisions directory. Recover REV 4 from commit 9583fb95aa2e5d3dda094dfc2341aa6d9e835722 (same path, retrievable from any worktree via git show) and land it in this story's diff. Do this as the LITERAL FIRST action of PLAN, before understanding_set - plan.md DependsOn only orders DEV-phase dispatch and cannot reach back into PLAN-phase timing. Read its section 0.0 FIRST: it records that sibling story B-506e has MERGED into main, which inverted an earlier provenance warning; rev 4 additionally corrects the consumer count to ten, downgrades the E5 row from a crash to a silent misread, and fixes a D-2 row that contradicted section 0.0.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/red-evidence-legacy-v1-record-validation-audit.md\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-008\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Land the decision document in docs/requirements/decisions/ so the story's own citations resolve\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The landed copy has no header text contradicting its own section 0.0 about which tree the citations describe.\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"It is landed before the PLAN scope review runs, not at the end of the