\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"After the fix, the same record set produces the same verdict regardless of the position of the malformed entry.\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Closes two scope gaps found by the PLAN scope reviewer (decision document acceptance rows V2 and E4), neither of which was owned by any item. V2: a valid v2 record must remain unchanged and continue to be correctly skipped by the v1 predicate - the v2 record union arrived on main with the B-506e merge, so this is live behaviour that a read-boundary validator could easily break by rejecting records it does not recognise. E4: an artifact whose records key is ABSENT must keep producing UNSATISFIED, which is the ordinary not-configured path and must NOT be reclassified as corruption; conflating absent with malformed would regress the very distinction this story exists to create. Both are regression assertions against behaviour that is correct today, not new capability.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-010\",\"relatedDocs\":[\".lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/background.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Assert the behaviour this fix must NOT change\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Absent and malformed remain distinguishable end to end: an absent artifact reports as not configured while a corrupt one reports as corrupt, at every consumer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"An artifact whose records key is ABSENT still produces UNSATISFIED via the ordinary not-configured path and is NOT reclassified as corruption.\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"A valid v2 record is still correctly skipped by the v1 predicate and its handling is unchanged from pre-fix.\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Closes the third scope gap: decision document section 10.5 requires that the validator ITSELF cannot throw on any JSON shape, and the checklist only pinned the specific enumerated malformed and envelope rows. Those rows were written from observed failures, so they prove the known cases and nothing about the unknown ones - which is the same mistake, in test form, that produced this defect in the first place. Generate arbitrary acyclic JSON values (nested objects and arrays, mixed primitives, empty containers, deeply nested structures, and objects with no prototype) and assert the validator returns a classification for every one of them and never throws. This is a property, not a case list.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-011\",\"relatedDocs\":[\".lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/background.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Fuzz the validator to prove it is total on arbitrary JSON\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The property is asserted over generated inputs rather than the enumerated failure rows, so it can catch shapes nobody thought to list - the same blind spot that produced this defect.\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Coverage includes empty containers, deeply nested structures, mixed primitive arrays, and objects created with no prototype.\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The validator returns a classification for arbitrary acyclic JSON values and never throws.\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}}],\"description\":\"On main at CLI 0.3.243 (after sibling story B-506e merged at 4d417a0c4b) a malformed VERSIONLESS record OR a malformed file envelope in a story's red-evidence.json still crashes the LIVE dev/review/done enforce gate with a bare TypeError instead of failing closed. B-506e closed only the unsupported-schemaVersion class (a null or string record now yields a typed error); the versionless-malformed class, array records, ordering-dependent silent corruption, and the ENTIRE file-envelope class remain live, verified by probe against current main. Root cause is unchanged: readJson is JSON.parse-and-cast with no validation between parse and the typed domain. Fix per the settled decisions in docs/requirements/decisions/red-evidence-legacy-v1-record-validation-audit.md (rev 3): full v1 validation at the read boundary covering envelope and records, malformed entries quarantined rather than thrown, the gate predicate kept total as defense-in-depth, and a mandatory migration scan proving no valid verdict moved. NOTE: re-locate every cited symbol against CURRENT main and never by line number - main advanced repeatedly during this story's INIT (0.3.239 to 0.3.243) and line citations from the original audit have drifted.\",\"headHash\":\"ee325a52e477f79d098a916789bd8079ca36571d\",\"materialHash\":\"5d50119277bbed5fb34d691776d9508645ad69ce5d720002c99a52967fb7d45a\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/red-evidence-legacy-v1-record-validation-audit.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence-artifact-validation.ts\",\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\",\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-migration-scan.mjs\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"packages/main/src/core/machine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proofstory.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/store.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/phase-gates.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/proofstory.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/red-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/story-review.ts\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/tests/red\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs\"]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"475faf4ee50969c442d7e527526546b7fdc4c5612cc8b61534d2b833bb3a5bde\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"4755f45fd1e95c6b86c73df0093eab3d299acc6488eb9770af1a9a3047c75b0f\",\"storyId\":\"B-2aa7\",\"title\":\"Validate the legacy v1 red-evidence artifact before enforce-gate evaluation\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.245\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-2aa7 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-2aa7\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-2aa7\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-2aa7\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n",
.lattice/story/actives/B-2aa7/review-runs.json:135:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"1400d1ed9c57c2ae45e7bb007a687cfa4b0a87a0badb77f929fb007ea0b7b1e3\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review implementation quality, safety, and maintainability.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-quality\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"ea63f5812defd28c23b8f6b9bdbcd058ac25cad6569484a85a15614e26a346f0\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Must FAIL on current main (CLI 0.3.243, after B-506e merged at 4d417a0c4b) before any fix exists. B-506e already closed ONE class - a record that is null or a bare string now yields a typed RedEvidenceSchemaError - so do NOT include those as RED rows; they would pass and prove nothing. RECORD class still live, each verified by probe: {id:'corrupt'} versionless with no observedFailure, observedFailure of null or 123, and an ARRAY record (typeof [] is 'object', so classifyRedRecordSchemaSafe still returns 'v1' for it). ORDERING: malformed-FIRST-then-satisfying, so Array.prototype.some cannot short-circuit past it. ENVELOPE class, wholly untouched by the merge: records as {} or 42 (non-iterable TypeError) and records as 'x' (which iterates the string's characters and misreports 'a record must be an object'). SILENT class, which is NOT a crash and therefore needs a different assertion: a JSON root of [], 'x', null or 42 returns the raw value and reads as ABSENT evidence everywhere, and an unparseable file lets a raw SyntaxError escape - assert the observable wrong behaviour, not a throw. Drive everything through proofStoryDiagnosticInput then evaluateProofStoryDiagnostics, the pair the live enforce gates call, never the predicate in isolation.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/\",\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Commit a repro-first RED artifact proving both crash classes still live on current main\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Each class asserts the right shape: CRASH rows assert a bare TypeError escapes, SILENT rows assert a wrong observable value AND no throw, and the unparseable-file row asserts a RAW untyped SyntaxError escapes rather than asserting no throw.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Rows that B-506e already closed (record is null or a bare string) are absent from the artifact, so no row passes vacuously.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The committed RED artifact runs on current main and FAILS, proving all three defect classes are live before any fix exists.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"SUPERSEDES the original plan to port a harness: packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs is now ON main (it arrived with the B-506e merge) and passes there, printing 2d584cc157e83ebb2f8396735f04d46946f0ba90d18a55d9fb2f263d706a11ec. That constant is therefore main's OWN pinned value, not a foreign import, and it must NOT be re-pinned. Run it BEFORE the fix to record that it passes on the pre-fix tree; that run is the baseline CHK-007 asserts against. Its five v1-only scenarios are empty store, satisfying record, blank-observedFailure record, foreign-acceptance-target record, and mixed store, each anchored by name so the digest cannot be silently re-pinned to a different verdict. Separately: 71c267a0a7372e9679d00b84be2e2b3480151bfa88939bddcae251aa750d95bc remains a phantom produced by no artifact (audit section 7.1) and must never be pinned.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Establish the pre-fix invariance baseline from main's existing five-scenario harness\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The pinned constant is not edited, and the phantom digest 71c267a0... appears nowhere as a pinned value.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The recorded baseline names the exact commit it was taken at, so a later reader can tell whether it predates the fix.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red-w2c-v1-verdict-invariance.mjs is run on the pre-fix tree and recorded as passing with digest 2d584cc1...\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Decision D-7. Full validation was chosen, so 'no valid verdict moved' is an assumption until this scan proves it - and the pinned digest CANNOT detect the difference, because all five of its scenarios are well-formed. Enumerate every reachable red-evidence.json in real story directories; for each record compute (current verdict, verdict under full v1 validation). The story may merge only if the differing set is empty, or every entry is individually justified in the story record. Report the count even when zero: 'scanned N artifacts, 0 affected' is the evidence; silence is not.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-migration-scan.mjs\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-migration-scan.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Run the mandatory migration scan over real story red-evidence artifacts and record the result\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The scan is re-runnable at merge time and does not hard-code the PLAN-phase snapshot of 105 artifacts / 144 records / 0 affected.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The scan reports its result even when the affected set is empty, so 'scanned N artifacts, 0 affected' is positive evidence rather than silence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The committed scan enumerates every reachable red-evidence artifact and reports a concrete count of records that satisfy the gate today while being schema-invalid.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Decisions D-1 to D-4. Precedence rule D-1 (which source of schema version wins): the FILE declares the era, the RECORD declares the exception, so a versionless record inside a v1-declared file is only CLAIMED v1 and must be validated against the v1 schema, never assumed to satisfy it. Validate the ENVELOPE before the records. Malformed entries are quarantined - records stays clean, malformed surface in a separate reported list - never thrown, never silently dropped. Mandatory v1 fields per the RedEvidenceRecord interface in core/types.ts (locate by symbol; the line range drifted). Cases that are easy to miss: a record missing only trigger / createdAt / id but otherwise complete is currently SATISFIED and is the WITNESS that full validation rather than the rejected narrow option was implemented; a prototype-inherited observedFailure (Object.create(null) and friends) must not be accepted via the prototype chain; and an ARRAY record must be rejected, since the classifier still returns 'v1' for it. Envelope rows from acceptance section 10.2.1: E5, a JSON root that is not an object ([], 'x', null, 42) currently does NOT crash - it flows through as the raw parsed value and every consumer reads it as ABSENT evidence, making a corrupt artifact indistinguishable from a missing one, which a crash-only validator would leave untouched; E6, a missing or unknown FILE-level schemaVersion must not silently degrade to v1; E7, an unparseable file currently lets a raw SyntaxError escape from readJson and must instead produce a typed error naming the path.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence-artifact-validation.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/store.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/red-b2aa7-artifact-validation.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDoc

